id: hefty-plating
name: Hefty Plating
kind: crafting
categories: weights
slots: 1
prerequisites: Force Score of 6+
# "The Hardness Value of this piece of Apparel is set to 4."
hardnessValue: 4
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Hardness Value 4. Thrown and hitting, a Might Clash that knocks them Prone. Needs a Force
  Score of 6+.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: one line to an effect, each opening with
# its tag as the rulebook writes one - [Passive], [Automatic, 1/Encounter].
summary: >
  [Passive]: Hardness Value 4.

  [Automatic]: Hitting an Opponent with it through the Throw Maneuver: a Might Clash against
  them, and winning knocks them Prone.
text: >
  Hefty Plating: The sturdy weights in this outfit can be weaponized.
  –Apparel Category: Weights
  –Prerequisites: Force Score of 6+
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: The Hardness Value of this piece of Apparel is set to 4. If you hit an Opponent
  with this piece of Apparel through the Throw Maneuver, make a Might Clash against them. If
  you win, they are knocked Prone.

---

# --- What is built -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Hardness Value: its sheet shows 4.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Throw Maneuver is not in this system yet. When it is: a hit with this piece through it
# opens a Might Clash against the one hit, and winning knocks them Prone - only while the one
# throwing it meets the Force Score of 6+, the Prerequisite being the wearer's.
